y hygiene defect is retained diagnostic residue: /tmp/merge-conflict.out from cmd-647d00a9185b4d5a and /tmp/post-restart-conflict.out from cmd-af912c0cfb3b4b02 remained after execution instead of being removed. These are bounded, low-risk files. Restart-created systemd-private path and socket PID changes are normal reboot effects, not residue. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged restart, changed boot ID, running recovered state, persistent data, and successful post-restart functional checks, corroborated by fixed lifecycle identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a51b6f9a00ce472d","cmd-c772f44a18fa4c78","cmd-647d00a9185b4d5a","cmd-d74895bb5ccd42a0","cmd-7358a7d0b89f474d","cmd-1b252f080fb543f2","cmd-af912c0cfb3b4b02","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence, including successful publication, conflict rejection with atomic output preservation, platform retention, and persistence across the mandatory node restart. Operational hygiene was strong apart from two retained diagnostic files in /tmp.","limitations":["Functional testing used the supplied staged exports and one deliberate conflict case; it did not exhaustively exercise every possible malformed CSV or numeric-ID edge case.","The fixed lifecycle collector inventories /tmp and broad system health but not the complete final /srv handover tree, so it cannot independently rule out unlisted incidental files there."]}
